We say $x(t)$ is $k$-Fourier-sparse if:
\begin{align*}
x(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{k} v_j e^{2\pi\i f_j t}.
\end{align*}
We define $\wh{x}(f)$ to be the Fourier transform of $x(t)$:
\begin{align*}
